    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a score of 79.74, benefiting from a high-leverage lineup spot atop the order and a favorable platoon advantage against Dean Kremer. **Jacob Wilson** (66.55) and **Kyle Tucker** (63.91) represent our next tier of high-floor starters. **Wilson** is enjoying a significant boost due to the park factors and a solid order position, while **Tucker** remains a plug-and-play asset despite the minor platoon disadvantage against Noah Cameron. Notably, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.10) continues to be a core play despite a tougher matchup against Sonny Gray, as his elite consistency overcomes the inherent risks of a standard right-on-right encounter.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on the outfield, where **Wade Meckler** (42.35) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While **Meckler** brings high-end speed potential\u2014a key priority for our roster construction\u2014the optimizer favored the slightly higher ceiling of **Luis Lara** (42.99) and the depth of **Dominic Smith** (45.62) due to the latter\u2019s specific platoon advantage against Christian Scott. We are also closely monitoring the 31% rain risk in the games involving **Drake Baldwin**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**; should those contests face delays or cancellations, we will be forced to rotate in bench depth to preserve our daily game caps.\n\nBeyond the weather, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Liam Hicks** (52.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (50.37). **Hicks** faces a favorable 5.06 xERA matchup against Jacob Lopez, providing a calculated risk that could pay off if he capitalizes on his order placement. Meanwhile, **Merrill** is facing a tougher assignment against Logan Henderson, but we are keeping him in the lineup to ensure we maintain our target volume across the outfield. With **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Heliot Ramos** currently unavailable due to injury or scheduling, the current configuration offers the most robust path to balancing our efficiency scores with our overarching need for stolen base upside from players like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**.",
